    "https://www.sfc.edu/student-life/center-for-career-exploration": {
      "title": "Search sfc.edu",
      "description": "Careers at the Plaza | St. Francis College Skip to main content Why SFC History & Mission Leadership Board of Trustees Careers at SFC Office of Belonging and Engagement SFC 170 | Five-Year Strategic Vision Mission, Ministry & Interfaith Dialogue Office of Institutional Effectiveness & Accreditation Contact Academics Browse Academic Divisions Business, Accounting & Entrepreneurship Science & Health Science Human Science, Sociocultural Studies & Social Justice Interdisciplinary Studies, Humanities & Education Browse Departments Browse Degree Type A-Z Prior Learning Credits & Equivalencies Career Pathways & Articulation Agreements General Education Program Academic Calendar Faculty Directory Online Learning Study Abroad Course Catalogue Library Grad School Admissions & Aid First Year Transfer International Scholarships & Affordability Student Financial Services Degree Completion Military Apply Now Visit SFC Admissions Calendar Request Information Alumni Alumni Association Affinity Groups Alumni Events Contact Us Alumni Events Dugan Memorial Golf Outing Charter Award Dinner Give to SFC Matching Gifts St. Francis Fund Senior Class Gift Student Life Student Life Accessibility and Accommodations Undergraduate Student Plaza Careers at the Plaza Center for Learning and Leadership ESports Opportunity Programs Student Health Student Community Pledge Campus Safety & Security Residence Life & Housing Purchase SFC Gear Tech Service Desk mySFC Portal The Office of Campus Life Registrar Self-Service Academic Policies News & Events News Social Directory Terrier Newsletter Events Brendan J. Dugan Memorial Golf Outing Charter Award Dinner Franciscan Month Volpe Lecture Series Office of Special Events Request Space Search site for programs, events, and more Make A Gift Apply Online Why SFC History & Mission Leadership Board of Trustees Office of Belonging & Engagement SFC 170 | Five-Year Strategic Vision Office of Institutional Effectiveness & Accreditation Careers at SFC Contact Academics Academic Divisions Business, Accounting & Entrepreneurship Human Science, Sociocultural Studies & Social Justice Interdisciplinary Studies, Humanities & Education Science & Health Science Browse Degree Type A-Z Prior Learning Credits and Equivalencies General Education Program Academic Calendar Course Catalogue Grad School Admissions & Aid Apply Online First Year Transfer International Scholarships & Affordability Degree Completion Military Visit SFC Admissions Calendar Contact Alumni Alumni Association Alumni Events Affinity Groups Give to SFC Contact Us Student Life Student Life Campus Safety & Security Purchase SFC Gear Student Health Mission, Ministry and Interfaith Dialogue Student Accounts Registrar Academic Policies The Office of Campus Life Tech Service Desk ESports News & Events News Social Directory Terrier Newsletter Events Make A Gift Apply Online Search sfc.edu Search Search Student Life Share Facebook X LinkedIn Email Print Careers at the Plaza SEARCH JOBS & INTERNSHIPS ON HANDSHAKE Shaping Successful Careers Careers at the Plaza, formerly the Center for Career Exploration, brings students and alumni together with employers and external partners to launch careers and foster talent. With our help, students explore, select and pursue meaningful careers while employers find recruiting plans and opportunities tailored to fit their needs. Your Career Portal Search Jobs & Internships on Handshake Handshake is the premier resource for St. Francis College students and alumni seeking jobs or internships. Careers at the Plaza How We Can Help Career-building at SFC is a community activity. At the Careers at the Plaza, we bring students and alumni together with faculty, staff and employers to forge lasting relationships that lead to successful, lasting careers. Students & Alumni Discover the right career path and get started with your job search Students & Alumni Employers & External Partners Tap into SFC's talent pool with a custom recruitment plan Employers Faculty & Staff Help guide students and alumni through the early career process Faculty & Staff Our Service Model Purpose We work with students and alumni through one-on-one, group advisement and workshops to: Explore majors and careers Gain Industry knowledge Discover self and career interests Preparation We help students and alumni to prepare for: Internships, part-time and full-time career opportunities Meaningful career exploration and experiences Partnership We partner with students, faculty, staff, employers and community members to: Develop talent pipelines Connect students with career opportunities Prepare for the ever-changing workforce Plan Ahead Graduate Student Advising Thinking of attending graduate or professional school? Each year, the Careers team leads a workshop to show the wide range of options available — even if your graduate school plans are a few years away. Contact our office through SFC's Handshake Portal or email us at [email protected] to schedule an appointment. Get In Touch Our Mission Statement Our mission is to ensure SFC students and alumni are career-ready for the workforce. How to Connect: For general inquiries or to connect with the Careers team, email us at [email protected] or call us at (718) 489-5360. You can also follow us on Instagram . Appointments for Students Schedule a career advisement appointment through SFC's Navigate App . Appointments for Alumni Schedule a career advisement appointment through SFC's Handshake Portal or email us at [email protected] . Academics SFC Online Student Life Alumni News & Events Apply Now Contact Us Admissions Give to SFC mySFC Portal Careers at SFC Consumer Information Stay Connected X Instagram Facebook YouTube TikTok LinkedIn RSS Visit St. Francis Schedule a Tour Request Space 179 Livingston Street Brooklyn, NY 11201-9902 (718) 522-2300 © St. Francis College, 2020–Present Privacy Policy Accessibility Statement Sexual Harassment Assault Response and Education Translate website language The College is in the process of reviewing and updating its website. The website is intended solely to provide general information as of the date of the publication. St. Francis College assumes no responsibility or liability for any errors or omissions and reserves the right to modify any information contained herein at any time. Please direct inquiries to the Office of Marketing & Communications at [email protected] back to top This site uses cookies We use cookies to improve user experience and analyze website traffic. By continuing to use this site, you agree to the use of cookies. Accept"
